rule.docs:
Summary

- Name: noUselessReturn
- Fix: safe
- Default severity: info
- Available from version: 2.3.15
- Diagnostic category: lint/complexity/noUselessReturn


Description

 Disallow redundant return statements.

 A `return;` statement with nothing after it is redundant when it is the
 last reachable statement in a function body. Removing it does not change
 the function's behavior, as execution naturally falls through to the end.

Examples

Invalid

 ```js,expect_diagnostic
 function foo() {
     return;
 }
 ```

 ```js,expect_diagnostic
 function foo() {
     doSomething();
     return;
 }
 ```

 ```js,expect_diagnostic
 function foo() {
     if (condition) {
         bar();
         return;
     }
 }
 ```

Valid

 ```js
 function foo() {
     return 5;
 }
 ```

 ```js
 function foo() {
     if (condition) {
         return;
     }
     bar();
 }
 ```

 ```js
 function foo() {
     for (const x of xs) {
         return;
     }
 }
 ```

